%U A053856 1379799701868277127827135922176,1779219416300608052895431535861170176
%N A053856 Number of n X n matrices over GF(4) of order dividing 2 (i.e., number of solutions of X^2=I in GL(n,4)).
%C A053856 Writing X = I + N, since GF(4) has characteristic 2, X^2 = I iff N^2 = 0. If rank(N) = r, then Im(N) is an r-dimensional subspace of Ker(N), with dim Ker(N) = n-r; choosing Ker(N), then Im(N) inside it, and finally an isomorphism V/Ker(N) -> Im(N) gives the formula below. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 06 2026
%D A053856 V. Jovovic, The cycle index polynomials of some classical groups, Belgrade, 1995, unpublished.
%H A053856 Kent E. Morrison, <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals/JIS/VOL9/Morrison/morrison37.html">Integer Sequences and Matrices Over Finite Fields</a>, Journal of Integer Sequences, Vol. 9 (2006), Article 06.2.1.
%F A053856 a(n) = Sum_{r=0..floor(n/2)} GaussianBinomial(n,r,4) * GaussianBinomial(n-r,r,4) * |GL(r,4)|. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 06 2026
%e A053856 a(2) = 1 + GaussianBinomial(2,1,4) * GaussianBinomial(1,1,4) * |GL(1,4)| = 1 + 5*1*3 = 16.
%Y A053856 Cf. A053722.
